  "tagline": "Open-source MPP warehouse forked from Greenplum and rebased on a newer PostgreSQL kernel.",
  "description": "Apache Cloudberry is an Apache Incubator project that continues the open-source Greenplum lineage after Broadcom closed Greenplum's code. Started by HashData in 2023 and donated to the ASF in 2024, it rebases the MPP architecture (coordinator plus segments, GPORCA optimizer, append-optimized columnar tables) on PostgreSQL 14 and adds features such as incremental materialized views, directory tables and PAX storage. It is the natural migration target for Greenplum 6/7 users wanting to stay open source; it is still incubating, with a young release history and community.",
